Every object would need a polySelf() method that may occasionally be called
by the interacting object. In case of hallucination (etc.) the dip method is
polymorphic "overloaded" by a function calling polySelf(), in case of the
polymorph potion the dip function would change the calling object (provide a
self reference as argument) by calling its own polySelf().

> Which object should contain this knowledge? This gets even more difficult
> if you're not sure what all the objects in the game are, as we were
> discussing previously.

Well, you *need* to know what objects there are in the game. You may always
provide some "nothing happens" function in the base class of every existing
nethack object class, so that at least the null-behaviour is not duplicated.

